TELEGRAM DESKTOP EXPORT

The export implementations in src/export/, src/export_archive.rs and
src/ported/tdexport_*.rs derive from the chat export in Telegram Desktop
(https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop, baseline tag v7.2.10,
Telegram/SourceFiles/export/), carried forward from this project's original
Python Desktop handoff. Copyright (C) the Telegram Desktop authors, licensed
under the GNU General Public License version 3 with an OpenSSL exception.
assets/tdexport/ (css/, js/, images/) retains the v7.2.10 export assets.

The native src/export/ implementation also incorporates the reviewed export
updates through Desktop v7.4.4 (bf4f714036f21c750d535dab199c811b3f9bfdd4).
src/export/assets/ and src/export/assets.rs retain the static export assets,
represented as Rust data where needed. Its CSS follows v7.4.4 with the
established emitted CRLF convention; JavaScript and all 42 PNG assets retain
their byte-identical v7.2.10/v7.4.4 content. These portions are included here
under GPLv3, the licence of this work. Their reviewed source and asset
provenance is recorded in tests/fixtures/tdexport-source-rust.json.

Photo thumbnails port Telegram Desktop's Qt 5.15.19 scaling and JPEG settings:
src/export/qt_scale.rs and src/ported/tdexport_qt_scale.rs port QImage's
SmoothTransformation (qtbase src/gui/painting/qimagescale.cpp and interpolate_4_pixels from
qdrawhelper_p.h), Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd., licensed under LGPL-3.0 /
GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0; the smooth-scaling code there is derived from
Imlib2 (Copyright (C) Carsten Haitzler and others; Daniel M. Duley), under its
BSD-style licence, whose notice is kept here. src/export/qt_jpeg.rs and
src/ported/tdexport_qt_jpeg.rs reproduce the settings of Qt's JPEG writer
(qjpeghandler.cpp). Encoding uses the native mozjpeg C library
(https://github.com/mozilla/mozjpeg; IJG, BSD-3-Clause and zlib licences,
including the libjpeg-turbo code it contains), through the mozjpeg 0.10.13
Rust wrapper (https://github.com/ImageOptim/mozjpeg-rust) and mozjpeg-sys 2.2.3
(https://github.com/kornelski/mozjpeg-sys), pinned in Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock.
An earlier native Rust export implementation used mozjpeg-rs at revision
6e58cd382d58f06e05764328c609d273ab4cf59f
(https://github.com/imazen/mozjpeg-rs); this is historical provenance, not the
current encoder dependency.

src/export/qt_icc.rs and src/ported/tdexport_qt_icc.rs port QtGui's matrix/TRC
ICC parser, color-space matrices, transfer curves and color-transform LUTs from Qt 5.15.19,
Copyright (C) 2016, 2018 The Qt Company Ltd., under the same GPL-3.0 option noted
above. Synthetic oracle fixtures were generated with that exact patched source;
no native Qt runtime is bundled or required by the Rust port.

src/export/jpeg_decoder/ adapts image-rs/jpeg-decoder 0.3.2
(https://github.com/image-rs/jpeg-decoder), Copyright (c) 2016 The jpeg-decoder
Developers, to reproduce the reference integer IDCT and chroma upsampling.
Its complete upstream MIT and Apache-2.0 notices remain alongside the adapted
source in LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE. This private Rust decoder is distinct
from the native mozjpeg encoder and the native decoder used by the older
src/ported/tdexport_qt_jpeg.rs path.

The vendored MTProto transport crates under vendor/grammers/ derive from
Lonami/grammers (https://codeberg.org/Lonami/grammers), dual-licensed under
MIT OR Apache-2.0; their upstream LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE files and
exact SHA-256 provenance manifests are retained in vendor/grammers/.


